Kernel Driver & DKMS Licensing Notice (GPL-2.0-only)
================================================================================

All Linux kernel module sources, DKMS patches, header definitions, and kernel
modifications located under `kernel-driver/` (including patches derived from
upstream `sound/soc/codecs/rt1316-sdw.c` and `sound/soc/codecs/rt1316-sdw-coeff-tables.h`)
are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 ONLY
(`SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only`), in strict compliance with upstream
Linux kernel licensing requirements.

A copy of the GNU General Public License version 2 is available at:
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html

Users installing the default userspace audio stack (`./install.sh --dsp-only`)
use exclusively MIT-licensed userspace components. Enabling the optional kernel
driver layer (`sudo ./install.sh --with-kernel`) builds and installs the
`GPL-2.0-only` DKMS module alongside the MIT userspace stack.
